============================================================
Lazarus Lessons Learned
============================================================

Lesson 001

Renaming a form manually may leave stale references inside
the project (.lpi).

After every rename:

• Check Project Inspector.
• Remove missing units.
• Add renamed unit.
• Perform Clean and Build.

Lesson 002

Unit search paths should be configured once at project level
instead of relying on individual file locations.

============================================================
Architectural Decisions
============================================================

The application will be organised as

Windows
    │
    ▼
TMainForm
    │
    ▼
TMView
    │
    ├── TConfig
    ├── TNavigator
    ├── TRenderer
    ├── TMouseEngine
    ├── TImageCache
    └── ...

TMainForm represents the Windows interface.

TMView represents the application itself.

============================================================
Design Decisions
============================================================

TMView becomes the central application object.

Responsibilities

• Create subsystem objects.
• Own subsystem objects.
• Destroy subsystem objects.
• Coordinate interaction.

TMView deliberately does NOT

• Display images.
• Load images.
• Navigate directories.
• Handle mouse input.

Those responsibilities belong to specialised classes.

============================================================
Object-Oriented Programming Notes
============================================================

Constructor

A constructor creates and initializes an object.

Example

    FMView := TMView.Create;

The constructor prepares the object for use.

------------------------------------------------------------

Fields

A field is a variable belonging to an object.

Example

    FConfig : TConfig;

A field stores either

• a value

or

• a reference to another object.

------------------------------------------------------------

Ownership

The object creating another object is normally responsible
for destroying it.

Example

TMView creates

    TConfig

Therefore

TMView also destroys

    TConfig

This ownership model will be used consistently throughout
MView.

============================================================
Coding Philosophy Reinforced
============================================================

The code should explain HOW.

Comments should explain WHY.

Architecture comes before implementation.

Small, specialised classes are preferred over large,
multi-purpose classes.

